<title>USA: FAA certifies new Embraer regional jet.</title>
<headline>FAA certifies new Embraer regional jet.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. aviation authorities on Monday officially certified the new 50-seat Embraer EMB-145 regional jet, allowing it to go into commercial service in the United States, the Brazilian company said.</p>
<p>Embraer said the twin-jet's certification by the Federal Aviation Administration followed 15 months of tests and more than 1,600 flying hours.</p>
<p>The firm said that on Wednesday it would deliver two of planes to Continental Express, the regional carrier of Continental Airlines Inc., and that two planes would be delivered on December 27.</p>
<p>It added that Continental, the plane's North American launch customer, had purchased 200 EMB-145s, with 25 firm orders for delvery through 1998 and options for 175 more over the next 12 years.</p>
</text>
